WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.840
The Anom-O-Tron 6000 - You know what it is
and what it does.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.800
Not too long ago, we had it simulate a battle
between the SCP Foundation and the slimy,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.200
sinister superhero Homelander, who terrorizes
the world of The Boys.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.490
And in the comments, we kept seeing one name
pop up: Omniman.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.269
The terrifying, almost unstoppable, Viltrumite
warrior who scared the hell out of all of

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:25.710
us in Invincible.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.900
So, we decided to run a simulation to see
if the SCP Foundation could find the same

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.970
success battling this diabolical corrupted
superman.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.160
The video you’re about to see is that simulation.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.380
Enjoy, and keep an eye on the skies!

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.059
It was unthinkable.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:47.399
Panic had spread throughout the Foundation
as reports came in that several of the most

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:52.559
high-profile groups of interest across the
globe had suffered unbearably brutal attacks

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:54.790
from an unknown assailant.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:59.859
Notable among the groups targeted were GOC
- Global Occult Coalition - as well as its

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.660
opposing organization: The Serpent’s Hand.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.820
In all incidents, key buildings belonging
to the groups were demolished, and the bodies

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.549
of all leadership personnel were discovered
beaten to a pulp.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:17.220
These massacres appeared to send a terrifying
message: whoever was behind these attacks,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.790
the Foundation was most likely next on the
chopping block.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.600
As all containment sites prepared for the
worst, it was Site 17 that received subsequent

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.200
news on the matter in the most unsettling
way imaginable.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.079
A small flying object was discovered in the
site’s airspace, and retrieved by an MTF-issue

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:35.079
helicopter.

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:40.670
The object appeared to be an action figure
of world-renowned superhero Omniman, and it

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.670
bore the trademark of Dr. Wondertainment Toys.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.899
The Mobile Task Force that discovered the
action figure had been on such high alert

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.990
that the appearance of this toy almost seemed
comical.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:55.240
There was uneasy laughter within the helicopter,
which immediately turned to silence when the

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.689
toy began to speak.

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:01.159
“Boys and girls, for the very first time,
Dr. Wondertainment presents to you … ‘Run!

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:02.850
Run for your lives!

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.810
Omniman is coming for all of us!’”

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:11.310
The toy continued what was apparently a prerecorded
voice over, which became increasingly frightened

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.530
and desperate as it went along.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.920
The contents of the recording confirmed that
the one responsible for the devastation of

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.310
the other groups of interest was none other
than Omniman himself.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.590
His reasons for doing this were unknown, but
he seemed adamant on wiping out all groups

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.470
with significant control over the planet’s
anomalies.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.090
Whoever was in charge at Dr. Wondertainment
had uncovered the truth shortly before Omniman

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.820
arrived to do the same to their group, and
had deployed the toy in a last ditch effort

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.720
to warn the SCP Foundation.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.780
It was an uncharacteristically opaque gesture
from the terrible toymaker, but the Foundation

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.150
had little choice but to take it seriously.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.370
If Earth’s most powerful superhero had really
gone rogue and was going after influential

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:01.909
organizations in some bid to eliminate competition,
the Foundation would have to develop appropriate

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:04.810
countermeasures as soon as possible.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.989
The first priority was securing the safety
of the 05 council, who would most likely be

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:12.190
the intended victims of Omniman’s rampage.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:17.650
Fortunately, their current location was extremely
classified, so rather than shuffle to a new

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.580
location, the council chose to stay where
they were.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:25.870
A conspicuous relocation process could inadvertently
give the game away, especially if the aptly

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.160
named “Aww, [Redacted] it!

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.780
Just launch us into Space!”

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.409
procedure was in-effect.

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:37.019
Omniman was known for his spacefaring capabilities,
and was fully capable of pursuing and boarding

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:40.659
the 05 council’s getaway shuttle if such
a thing was attempted.

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:46.150
Additionally, there would be no movement of
forces to the location of the 05 council.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.180
Mobile Task Forces that were already in the
field would be instructed to immediately cease

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.689
their current mission and focus on locating
Omniman.

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:58.640
While the superhero was incredibly dangerous,
it was paramount that valuable time was bought

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.519
so that a better attack plan could be formulated.

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:05.740
That was one advantage the Foundation had
over most of the other groups of interest:

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.970
the reserves to prolong a war of attrition,
no matter how strong the enemy was.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.940
There was also the matter of establishing
protections for Site-17, since Wondertainment

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:20.579
had sent the action figure there of all places
to deliver the message, it was likely that

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:23.259
Omniman would be headed there first.

00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:28.190
Site staff requested the immediate transfer
of the infamous Mobile Task Force Tau-5 Samsara

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:31.980
- a unit of immortal cyborgs with superhuman
physiology.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.840
While Omniman was known to have fought and
defeated everything from the spawn of ancient

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:42.730
gods, to cyborgs, to immortals: The four members
of samsara were all three and had strength

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.030
in numbers.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.610
The request remained pending for several minutes,
causing one researcher to blithely remark

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.039
that the 05 council had probably called dibs.

00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:55.780
Fearing that MTF Tau-5 wouldn’t arrive in
time to intercept Omniman, the researchers

00:04:55.780 --> 00:05:00.310
assessed which anomalies contained on site
would be best suited to holding the superhero

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.310
back.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:08.100
One keter-class SCP in particular immediately
came to mind: SCP-4051 - a male humanoid with

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.910
the anomalous ability to create extradimensional
wormholes.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:17.949
These wormholes could be used to produce any
object that SCP-4051 desired, including exceedingly

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:20.050
unstable cognitohazards.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:25.860
While SCP-4051’s powers were certainly formidable,
it was the fact that the humanoid - who went

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:31.170
by the name Rainer Miller - had previously
been acting as a vigilante in the United States.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:36.450
In other words, Rainer Miller was likely to
be of special interest to Omniman - even if

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:40.170
that interest merely amounted to having one
more target to wipe out.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:45.510
While it wouldn’t be the only humanoid SCP
that could be considered similar to a superhero,

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:48.919
4051 was definitely the closest at hand.

00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:53.470
Not too long after the discussion took place,
the site radars began to pick up on Omniman

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.530
closing in.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:59.229
His approach was extraordinarily fast, breaking
through the sound barrier, and landing with

00:05:59.229 --> 00:06:01.950
great force in the center of Site-17.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:07.699
There was no time to waste, and all available
guards and Mobile Task Forces personnel were

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:11.919
ordered to zero-in on Omniman’s location
and open fire.

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:16.789
As one might expect, bullets weren’t exactly
effective against the superhero-turned-serial

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:21.699
killer, but they did provide a plausible distraction
while the researchers mobilized to find other

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:24.160
means of neutralizing Omniman.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:29.040
It was a terrifying sight watching the costumed
man stand there within the hail of bullets,

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:33.639
bearing no outward signs of distress aside
from a stern facial expression.

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:38.360
He moved smoothly through the air towards
the nearest soldier and shattered every rib

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.560
with a single punch.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.169
He then grabbed another and used him to bludgeon
several other agents.

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:49.030
Even with the substantial advantage in raw
power, there was a considered tactical reason

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.960
for each of Omniman’s movements.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.420
He systematically made his way through the
site, crushing all within his path with absolute

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.479
prejudice.

00:06:57.479 --> 00:07:00.690
There were going to be no survivors if this
continued.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:05.210
Fortunately, one of the Site-17 other contingencies
was about to come into play.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:09.389
You see, The Foundation had done their research,
and with the corroboration of information

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:13.539
from other groups including the United States
government had deduced that Omniman might

00:07:13.539 --> 00:07:17.020
have a psychological weakness that could be
exploited.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:23.479
Namely, his teenage son Mark - otherwise known
by his superhero alias Invincible.

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:27.900
While the Foundation was far too cautious
to directly contact Invincible - mostly out

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:33.700
of fear that the boy could be an accomplice,
the next best thing could still stall Omniman

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.699
- and give the researchers a chance to get
SCP-4051 ready for combat.

00:07:38.699 --> 00:07:43.180
It certainly took Omniman by surprise when
he was floating down one of the newly blood-soaked

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:47.129
corridors and saw Invincible standing at the
end, staring him down.

00:07:47.129 --> 00:07:48.129
“Dad?

00:07:48.129 --> 00:07:49.500
What is going on?

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.440
Why are you hurting them?” said what appeared
to be Mark.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.990
Omniman stopped in place and his expression
changed a look of concern.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.690
For the first time since he had arrived at
Site 17, Omniman spoke.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.690
“Mark?”

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.129
“Come on, Dad, this is crazy!

00:08:03.129 --> 00:08:05.110
You should stop this and go back home to mom!”

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.080
Omniman furrowed his brow.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.440
Something was off here.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.610
For one, this version of Invincible had both
feet on the ground, even though he would have

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.590
all the same powers of his father.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:19.169
Also, the fact that Invincible hadn’t approached
suggested that this individual was in such

00:08:19.169 --> 00:08:22.669
fear of Omniman that it refused to approach.

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:26.810
Omniman had been caught off guard by this
at first, worried that his son could be afraid

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.860
of him to this extent, but it was starting
to seem suspicious.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:36.050
Mark was no coward - he had become a superhero
like his father because he wanted to protect

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:38.310
the world from all manner of threats.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:42.830
Although the difference in combat experience
between the two was vast, Omniman knew that

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.959
the Invincible he knew was reckless enough
to challenge him or at least have this conversation

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:49.920
at a regular distance.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:56.050
His intuition was right on the money as this
was not Invincible at all, but SCP-953 - the

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.089
polymorphic humanoid - instead.

00:08:58.089 --> 00:09:03.379
While this keter-class SCP was known for taking
many forms - usually that of beautiful women

00:09:03.379 --> 00:09:09.180
- the Foundation staff had given it access
all available information on Omniman and Invincible’s

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:15.170
father-son relationship and in doing so successfully
convinced it that taking the form of Omniman’s

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:20.370
son was the best path the self-preservation
during this perilous scenario.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:26.279
SCP-953 continued to make attempts at talking
Omniman, doing its best to remain still - not

00:09:26.279 --> 00:09:31.330
wanting to reveal the vulpine features beneath
the Invincible costume it was wearing.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.200
But Omniman proved to be too clever for this
gambit.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:38.910
He chuckled, then suddenly zoomed forward
with his fist raised in front of him.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:44.010
SCP-953 flinched in terror, only to find that
Omniman had pulled his punch.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:50.079
At first, SCP-953 was relieved to still be
intact but this soon dissipated as the humanoid

00:09:50.079 --> 00:09:54.980
looked at Omniman and found none of the compassion
that was on his face just moments ago.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.620
“You’re not Mark,” Omniman said.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.930
“He’s stronger than this.”

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.940
SCP-953 trembled in fear.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:06.620
The polymorphic humanoid only had one card
left to play, and it prayed that it worked.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:11.130
953 shapeshifted again, this time into Omniman’s
wife Debbie.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:15.151
Her fox-like features were more pronounced
in this form, but it was clear that the sight

00:10:15.151 --> 00:10:18.930
of his human partner’s face made Omniman
hesitant to attack.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:23.100
This hesitation was all the time that the
polymorphic humanoid needed to run away, as

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:28.850
several guards and SCP-4051 arrived to take
over the duty of stalling Omniman.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:33.010
Several wormholes opened up around Omniman,
deploying sonic grenades which stunned him

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.579
for several seconds.

00:10:34.579 --> 00:10:38.920
The guards unleashed all their ammo, and drew
Omniman’s aggression while Rainer prepared

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:44.590
his next weapon - a wormhole to a pocket dimension
filled with flamethrowers, which he directed

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:49.680
at Omniman, hoping to at least cause some
lasting pain if not proper burns.

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:55.250
The flames did temporarily obscure his vision,
but they didn’t hinder him for long as Omniman

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:00.380
moved straight upwards through the ceiling
before descending back down into the building,

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.760
massacring the guards surrounding SCP-4051.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:07.990
He looked on Rainer with disdain, especially
as the humanoid opened a wormhole and pulled

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:09.820
out an aluminum baseball bat.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:13.310
“You really think that piece of earthling
sports equipment is going to do anything to

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.310
me?”

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.310
Omniman said.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:17.120
“It doesn’t matter if it does or doesn’t.”

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.120
Rainer replied.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:22.090
“You’re not the hero you once were, and
someone has to try and stop you.”

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.190
Omniman paused, reminded of his own son.

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:28.910
Though mere sentiment wouldn’t be to spare
Rainer Miller the fate of the rest of his

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:29.930
planet and its people.

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.910
Omniman went in for the kill, but Rainer opened
a wormhole directly in front of himself, which

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:37.800
contained multiple anti-tank rifles that fired
in Omniman’s direction.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.180
The impact didn’t phase Omniman, but it
slowed the superhero down just enough for

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.380
Rainer to tuck and roll behind him.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:48.339
Rainer reached into another wormhole for a
gas-mask which he quickly donned as another

00:11:48.339 --> 00:11:52.220
one of his wormholes unleashed deadly poison
gas into the corridor.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:57.240
Omniman held his breath and flew towards Rainer,
grabbing his aluminum bat mid-swing and bending

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.519
it into an L-shape without any apparent effort.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:04.760
Rainer let go of his weapon, but Omniman quickly
grabbed him by the wrist and lifted him into

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.899
the air before slamming him down to the ground.

00:12:07.899 --> 00:12:13.770
Rainer Miller - SCP-4051 - was incapacitated,
perhaps fatally.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:17.860
Before Omniman could confirm his kill - he
was tackled and immediately thrown through

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:22.829
the nearest wall by the combined force of
four individuals in cybernetic armor.

00:12:22.829 --> 00:12:28.310
Mobile Task Force Tau-5 Samsara had arrived,
and together, they surrounded Omniman and

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.380
hit him with everything they had.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:36.339
Punches and kicks bombarded him from all angles,
offering barely any window for a response.

00:12:36.339 --> 00:12:40.769
The formation didn’t last long, as Omniman
withstood the hits and maneuvered behind one

00:12:40.769 --> 00:12:46.149
of the members of Samsara, grabbing and snapping
the cyborgs neck in one quick motion.

00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:50.510
One of its fellows swung for Omniman’s face
only for him to catch the blow and severely

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:54.050
batter the arm of the attacker - rendering
it unusable.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:58.089
Omniman grabbed the last two members by the
throats and squeezed until he heard the familiar

00:12:58.089 --> 00:13:00.990
pop and crack, then he let their bodies fall.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:04.830
Of course, this wasn’t enough to neutralize
Samsara completely.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:10.790
The cyborgs were down, but not out - as their
fast regeneration began to fix their injuries.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:15.709
With detached contempt, Omniman stomped forcefully
on their heads - shattering the skulls of

00:13:15.709 --> 00:13:18.120
each member of Samsara one by one.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.070
That should be a lot harder to fix.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.540
Omniman thought to himself.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:26.350
He was almost finished here, then it would
be on to the next containment site, and eventually

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.470
to the 05 council itself.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:33.089
His planet wouldn’t need meddlesome groups
like the SCP Foundation - made up of inferior

00:13:33.089 --> 00:13:35.079
humans playing at civilization.

00:13:35.079 --> 00:13:40.079
He’d make sure they knew how powerless they
were before the rest of the people of Viltrum

00:13:40.079 --> 00:13:42.760
arrived to complete the conquest of Earth.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:47.399
He applauded the short-lived bravery of Rainer
Miller, and in an uncharacteristic moment

00:13:47.399 --> 00:13:52.720
of mercy, chose not to go back and check if
his previous opponent had truly been killed.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:57.940
Omniman rationalized that he already inflicted
a killing blow, but deep down - as he concluded

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:03.100
his rampage through Site 17 and departed for
the site of his next slaughter - he knew that

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:06.850
he subconsciously gave the boy a chance to
live.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:09.170
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:12.760
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:16.589
Now go check out “Could Homelander's Ego
Crush The SCP Foundation?”

00:14:16.589 --> 00:14:21.930
and “SCP-076 Able VS Chainsaw Man...Who
Has The Most Lethal Weapon?”

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.740
for more crossovers with the world’s wildest
superheroes!

